{"key": "g01", "title": "Particles of the Qur'an 1: The Prepositions", "subtitle": "Twelve small words that change the noun after them", "trigger_at": "2026-11-03T13:00:00.000Z", "body": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "captionedImage", "content": [{"type": "image2", "__img": "cover-g01.png", "alt": "Particles of the Qur'an 1: The Prepositions"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Particles of the Qur'an, part 1 of 5", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Arabic has three kinds of word: nouns, verbs and particles ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "huroof", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", حُرُوف). Particles are the small words: \"in\", \"from\", \"not\", \"that\", \"so\". They are few, but they are everywhere, and many of them change the ending of the next word. This short series goes through them one group at a time."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"textAlign": null, "level": 3}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Two kinds of particle"}]}, {"type": "bullet_list", "content": [{"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Active particles", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "al-huroof al-'aamilah", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", الْحُرُوفُ الْعَامِلَةُ, \"the working particles\"): they change the case of the noun after them (nominative, accusative, genitive) or the mood of the verb after them (indicative, subjunctive ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "mansoob", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", مَنْصُوب), jussive)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Inactive particles", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "al-huroof ghayr al-'aamilah", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", الْحُرُوفُ غَيْرُ الْعَامِلَةِ, \"the non-working particles\"): they add meaning but change no endings."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"textAlign": null, "level": 3}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The prepositions"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The first group of active particles are the prepositions, "}, {"type": "text", "text": "huroof al-jarr", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " (حُرُوفُ الْجَرِّ, \"the pulling particles\"). The noun after a preposition is genitive: it usually ends in kasra. The preposition and its noun together are called "}, {"type": "text", "text": "jaar wa majroor", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " (جَارّ وَمَجْرُور, \"the puller and the pulled\")."}]}, {"type": "ordered_list", "attrs": {"start": 1, "type": null, "order": 1}, "content": [{"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "with, in:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " بِ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "bi", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). بِسْمِ اللَّهِ \"in the name of Allah\" (1:1)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "by (an oath, with Allah only):", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " تَ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "ta", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). تَاللَّهِ \"by Allah\" (12:85)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "like:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " كَ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "ka", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). مَثَلُ نُورِهِ كَمِشْكَاةٍ فِيهَا مِصْبَاحٌ \"the example of His light is like a niche in which there is a lamp\" (24:35)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "for, to:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " لِ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "li", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). فَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ \"so pray to your Lord\" (108:2)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "by (an oath):", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " وَ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "wa", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). وَالنَّازِعَاتِ غَرْقًا \"by those who pull out violently\" (79:1)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "far be it:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " حَاشَا ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "haashaa", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "), shortened in the Qur'an to حَاشَ. حَاشَ لِلَّهِ \"Allah forbid!\" (12:31)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "from:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " مِنْ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "min", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). الْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ \"the foundations of the House\" (2:127)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "about:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " عَنْ ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "'an", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). عَنِ النَّعِيمِ \"about the blessings\" (102:8)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "on, upon:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " عَلَى ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "'alaa", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). وَإِنَّهُ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكَ لَشَهِيدٌ \"and he is a witness to that\" (100:7)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "until:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " حَتَّى ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "hattaa", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). حَتَّىٰ زُرْتُمُ الْمَقَابِرَ \"until you visit the graves\" (102:2)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "in:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " فِي ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "fee", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ \"in this world and the Hereafter\" (2:220)."}]}]}, {"type": "list_item", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "to, towards:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " إِلَى ("}, {"type": "text", "text": "ilaa", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "). وَإِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَارْغَبْ \"and to your Lord turn all your attention\" (94:8)."}]}]}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"textAlign": null, "level": 3}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One thing to notice"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Look at the noun right after each preposition: اسْمِ \"name\", نُورِهِ \"His light\", مِشْكَاةٍ \"a niche\", رَبِّكَ \"your Lord\", الْبَيْتِ \"the House\", النَّعِيمِ \"the blessings\", الْمَقَابِرَ \"the graves\". All end in kasra except the last. الْمَقَابِرَ \"graves\" is a plural pattern that never takes kasra, so its genitive is shown with a fatha. You will meet these nouns again later."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Next:", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " the four particles that change the ending of a verb from "}, {"type": "text", "text": "-u", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " to "}, {"type": "text", "text": "-a", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": "."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "From my book", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " Quran Grammar Summary "}, {"type": "text", "text": "(second edition), section 1.5.", "marks": [{"type": "em"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"textAlign": null}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Download this post as a PDF", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", with all the Arabic in Qur'anic script: "}, {"type": "text", "text": "Particles of the Qur'an 1: The Prepositions (PDF)", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://www.seemabooks.com/downloads/substack-posts/g01-the-prepositions.pdf", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow", "class": null}}]}]}]}}